      "status": "fixed",
      "status_notes": "CVE-2025-67030 (GHSA-6fmv-xxpf-w3cw): Expand.extractFile() in plexus-utils did not confine extracted entries to the target directory, allowing directory traversal from a crafted archive. plexus-utils before 3.6.1 (and 4.0.0 before 4.0.3) is affected; 3.6.1 carries the fix (https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-6fmv-xxpf-w3cw, https://github.com/codehaus-plexus/plexus-utils/issues/294, https://github.com/codehaus-plexus/plexus-utils/pull/296). We read every jar, nested jars included, in every published gradle-8 package for Alpine 3.23 in the DHI Alpine repository, 16 versions from 8.14.4-r0 to 8.14.8-r0, after verifying each package against its index checksum; the x86_64 and aarch64 packages of each version have the same checksum, and 8.14.5-r4 is published for x86_64 only. Gradle ships plexus-utils as /usr/share/java/gradle/lib/plugins/plexus-utils-<version>.jar, and no other jar in these packages contains plexus-utils classes, relocated or not. By the Maven metadata inside that jar, builds 8.14.4-r0 and 8.14.4-r1 ship plexus-utils 3.5.1, and 8.14.4-r2 and every later build ship 3.6.1. The range ends at 8.14.4-r2."
