      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:apk/dhi/gradle-9@9.4.0-r0?distro=dhi-3.23"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:apk/dhi/gradle-9@9.4.0-r1?distro=dhi-3.23"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:apk/dhi/gradle-9@9.4.1-r1?distro=dhi-3.23"
        }
      ],
      "status": "affected",
      "action_statement": "Update gradle-9 to 9.4.1-r2 or later.",
      "status_notes": "CVE-2025-67030 (GHSA-6fmv-xxpf-w3cw): Expand.extractFile in plexus-utils before 3.6.1 (and 4.0.0 to 4.0.2) does not stop archive entries from escaping the target directory. It is fixed in plexus-utils 3.6.1 and 4.0.3 (https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-6fmv-xxpf-w3cw, https://github.com/codehaus-plexus/plexus-utils/issues/294). Read every published gradle-9 package for Alpine 3.23 in the DHI Alpine repository, 9.4.0-r0 to 9.9.2-r0 (22 versions; 9.6.1-r3 and 9.6.1-r4 are published for x86_64 only, and each aarch64 package has the same index checksum as its x86_64 package), verified against the index checksum, and opened every jar, including jars nested in jars, taking each library version from the Maven metadata inside the jar, not from the file name. The only copy of plexus-utils is usr/share/java/gradle/lib/plugins/plexus-utils-<version>.jar: it is 3.5.1 in 9.4.0-r0 to 9.4.1-r1 and 3.6.1 from 9.4.1-r2 to 9.9.2-r0, and its org/codehaus/plexus/util/Expand.class is byte-identical to the one in the plexus-utils 3.5.1 and 3.6.1 jars on Maven Central respectively. No other jar in any of these builds carries a relocated copy of plexus-utils. The range ends at 9.4.1-r2."
    },
